/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Utils Utils
 * @ingroup Foundation
 * @brief Low-level move, swap, and program-memory helpers.
 *
 * Utils provides the small operations needed by Foundation containers without
 * requiring `<utility>`, plus the program-memory access used by constant
 * tables on AVR. The public surface consists of Move, Swap, and, since 1.4.0,
 * Flash; empty historical placeholders were removed before the API freeze.
 *
 * @section FoundationUtilsHeaders Public Headers
 *
 * | Need | Header |
 * | ---- | ------ |
 * | Entire Foundation library | `#include <Foundation.h>` |
 * | Entire Utils module | `#include <Foundation_Utils.h>` |
 * | Nested module umbrella | `#include <Foundation/Utils.h>` |
 * | Move only | `#include <Foundation/Utils/Move.h>` |
 * | Swap only | `#include <Foundation/Utils/Swap.h>` |
 * | Program-memory data only | `#include <Foundation/Utils/Flash.h>` |
 *
 * @section FoundationUtilsUsage Basic Usage
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * int first = 3;
 * int second = 9;
 * Foundation::Utils::Swap(first, second);
 *
 * MoveOnly destination(Foundation::Utils::Move(source));
 * @endcode
 *
 * Move performs an rvalue cast; it does not move data by itself. The selected
 * constructor or assignment operator defines the resulting transfer and the
 * valid state of the moved-from object. Swap requires move construction and
 * move assignment compatible with the supplied type. Move itself is
 * `constexpr` and `noexcept`; Swap does not promise `noexcept` because the
 * selected type's move operations may throw.
 *
 * @section FoundationUtilsFlash Program-Memory Data
 *
 * AVR is a Harvard architecture: an ordinary `const` table is copied from
 * flash into the small RAM at startup. `FOUNDATION_FLASH` expands to `PROGMEM`
 * on AVR and to nothing elsewhere, and `Foundation::Utils::Flash` reads the
 * data back identically on every target:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * const uint16_t Table[] FOUNDATION_FLASH = {100, 250, 400};
 * const char Name[] FOUNDATION_FLASH = "Foundation";
 *
 * uint16_t value = Foundation::Utils::Flash::Read(&Table[1]);
 * char buffer[8];
 * size_t length = Foundation::Utils::Flash::CopyString(buffer, sizeof(buffer), Name);
 * @endcode
 *
 * Only namespace-scope `const` objects of trivially copyable types may be
 * placed with `FOUNDATION_FLASH`, and on AVR they must never be dereferenced
 * directly. `Read` returns a RAM copy, `Copy` transfers raw bytes, and
 * `CopyString` follows `snprintf` semantics: it always terminates a non-empty
 * buffer and returns the full source length so truncation can be detected.
 * Placement is verified by linking `tests/AvrConsumer`, whose flash table and
 * string appear in `.text` rather than `.data`.
 *
 * @section FoundationUtilsExample Runnable Examples
 *
 * `Foundation_Utils_MoveAndSwap` demonstrates swapping integers and moving a
 * non-copyable object. `Foundation_Utils_FlashData` reads a table entry and
 * copies a string from program memory. See @ref Foundation_Examples "Examples" for build and
 * launch instructions.
 */

/**
 * @namespace Foundation::Utils
 * @ingroup Foundation_Utils
 * @brief Low-level move, swap, and program-memory helpers.
 */
